 "notes": "Solid 'this work' curve of Fig. 4 (1-sigma limit on (g_p^n)^2/4pi vs boson mass m in meV), digitized from the vector EPS axionlimitMore_g2.eps in the arXiv e-print; axis calibration from tick-mark coordinates, cross-checked against the quoted massless limit (g_p^n)^2/4pi < 5.8e-10 (flat level reproduces it to <1%) and the reference lines at 2.5e-8 (gravity, ref [6]) and 2.3e-5 (Ramsey). Converted via g_an = sqrt(4pi * y) and m_eV = 1e-3 * m_meV. The paper's derivative coupling L = (g_p/2M_n) psibar gamma^mu gamma5 psi d_mu phi matches the canonical g_an normalization exactly, so no 2m_N factor is needed. The curve is non-monotonic: a sharp spike to g_an~4e-3 at m~1.5e-6 eV and a dip to ~7e-4 near 2e-6 eV (geometric cancellation of the dipole-dipole potential), then rises off the top of the plot at ~6.5e-6 eV. Limit is on the neutron coupling only (87% neutron polarization in 3He assumed by the paper); confidence level is 1 sigma (~68%) as stated. Not a dark-matter search, so no density assumption.",
